WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.968
We've just got some news in to us.

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.870
Another earthquake has struck

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.139
the Turkish-Syrian border region.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.240
Now, at this point in time,

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.343
we understand it has a magnitude of 6.4.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.178
We don't have any other details

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.147
at this stage about the damage.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.182
This, of course, comes two weeks

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.550
after that devastating earthquake

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.587
that killed more than 47,000 people

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.322
and left mass destruction

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.623
across that area.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.658
I want to go to Adana, Turkey,

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:26.192
where I'm not

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.328
a bus here is standing by nada.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:28.895
We're just getting

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.097
some very brief information into us.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:31.598
But I understand

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:34.601
you've been speaking again to survivors

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:35.468
of that major earthquake

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.303
from from two weeks ago.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.972
I can't imagine how traumatized

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.273
many more people are

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:43.943
with another earthquake having just hit

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:45.745
Linda,

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:46.546
it is

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.748
astonishing that people here are still,

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.917
of course, reeling from this earthquake.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:51.785
And now

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:54.854
there is news of another earthquake, 6.4,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.723
according to the Emergency

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.725
Disaster Management Authority

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.793
here in Turkey.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.628
Epicenter so far reported

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:02.796
in the province of Hatay,

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.631
which was one of the hardest hit

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:06.199
by this month's earthquake.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.700
Some 80% of the buildings

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.803
that collapsed about to collapse

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:11.004
or have been deemed

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.073
necessary of demolition

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.808
because they are simply so unsafe.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.943
And I have to say, here in Adana,

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.244
we have quite a way away

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:18.878
from that

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:19.846
epicenter reported

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:22.115
just in the last half hour or so.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.950
And we felt the tremor

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.752
to the extent that this entire hotel

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.220
that we're currently in at the moment

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.488
evacuated the building,

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:30.323
many rushing out, children

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.591
being pulled out of fear.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.992
And you can imagine the trauma,

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.260
the emotional trauma

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.162
that these people in southeastern Turkey

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.530
have already been through.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.699
So much loss, so much destruction.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.734
There is still so much

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.937
fear here in southeast Turkey.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:46.072
So to go through that again

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.041
is difficult to explain.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.609
And we felt it over here.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.111
But of course, it is reported

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.112
that that epicenter

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:52.745
of the

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.347
worst of the tremors was felt

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.215
further east

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.283
towards Gaziantep and Hearts.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.651
And we are still learning

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.619
more details about this,

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.154
still waiting for more information

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:02.789
from the authorities

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.090
regarding the extent

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.391
of this latest quake,

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.427
the extent of the potential destruction

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:08.461
and damage.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.296
This may or may not have caused.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.164
But, of course,

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.899
there is a real sense of urgency,

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:13.800
growing pressure

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.901
on the Turkish government

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.202
and authorities,

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.770
a real sense of fear here

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.906
among the Turkish population.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:20.940
And of course, there's already

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.041
been so much devastation

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.910
so much destruction.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.811
And we are learning

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.045
that the Turkish authority

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.714
is trying to step up,

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.182
called for accountability.

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:30.683
They are carrying out an investigation

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.719
into reports of building codes,

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.921
not being respected or enforced properly.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.457
So far, more than 400 people identified

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.558
as potential suspects.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:41.127
At least 120 people arrested.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.662
And we're talking about the destruction

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.030
and the devastation.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.499
More than 100,000 buildings

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.701
have been so far examined

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:49.502
and have been deemed

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.970
as requiring the demolition

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.338
of already collapsed.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.940
And there are still hundreds

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.275
more thousands of buildings

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:57.443
to be assessed and evaluated.

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:58.811
So this is a significant feat

00:02:58.811 --> 00:02:59.746
for the Turkish government.

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:00.813
And this latest

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:01.814
term of this latest quake

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.017
is only going to add to that.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.251
And we've been speaking

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.053
to some of those impacted

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.288
by the earthquake.

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:10.823
Some of them have already been evacuated

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:12.392
to other parts of the city,

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:14.527
including in Istanbul,

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:15.361
where we were able to meet with

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.329
some of the children

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.598
who have sadly lost their loved ones

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:19.732
and separated from families.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.067
Some have lost their parents

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.136
and their names still unknown.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:23.736
Take a look.

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:26.472
The laughter

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:29.342
hides their loss pulled from the rubble.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.644
The parents still missing

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.479
the identities of some.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.847
A mystery.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.450
This orphanage has become home to

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.918
some of Turkey's youngest

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.020
earthquake survivors.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:41.621
Authorities

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:42.488
say the search

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.724
for living relatives continues,

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.226
but some of these children

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:49.162
are believed to have lost everyone

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.530
in better children.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.198
When we first received these children,

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:52.765
we observed

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:55.034
signs of post-traumatic stress disorder.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.003
The children were very fragile.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.638
So as well as providing shelter

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.273
and security to these kids,

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.407
we also began providing

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:04.143
psychosocial support

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.512
outside the devastation wrought by

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.247
the earthquake

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.848
has left countless children

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:09.616
orphaned

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:12.752
or separated from their loved ones.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.821
And while authorities say they are so far

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.155
managed to reunite more

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.324
than 900 children with their families,

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.060
many are still waiting to be processed.

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:22.328
And NGOs

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:22.962
fear that

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.397
millions could be at risk

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.933
of acute psychological distress.

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.901
They already have their loved ones lost.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.137
They already have their homes lost.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:32.972
They already have their schools lost.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:35.141
All schools are gone.

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:37.410
But if they also lose their hopes,

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.113
that means loss of generations.

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:41.981
That loss

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:42.515
is all

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.550
too familiar to this Syrian family.

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:47.620
Three generations now temporarily hosted

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.656
in this small one bed apartment

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:50.857
in Istanbul.

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.292
Their home in Antakya,

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.193
now a mountain of rubble

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.061
26 year old

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:57.163
Raghad says she was the first week

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:58.865
when the earthquake struck,

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.366
pulling her mother and forces

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:01.501
to safety

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.670
just moments before their home collapsed.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.039
When the earthquake happened.

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:09.008
I, I think it's your judgment day.

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:09.842
Yes.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:13.112
That is a very a very big sound

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:16.115
that it's not going out from my head.

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:19.485
Every time it's your window here.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:20.586
Yes.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:23.222
But this is not the first time

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.424
Raghad and her family

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:27.093
have face a tragedy of this magnitude.

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:29.762
Originally from the Syrian city of Homs,

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:30.997
the constant

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:32.265
barrage of airstrikes

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:33.066
forced the family

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.134
to flee their home in 2014.

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:36.703
But having her life

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:38.604
upended by catastrophe

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:40.540
time and time again

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.240
has taken its

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.376
toll on their mental health.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:45.078
That's not my first time.

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:47.780
I get a life from a war or something bad.

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:50.049
And every time I said, why

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.319
I'm not why, I'm asking myself, why?

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.021
Why am I life?

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:56.522
Maybe it was easy.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.591
If I am not,

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.927
then easier than going through it.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.462
Yes, because it's not

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:04.831
my first time that I start from zero.

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:07.800
Starting from 04.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.737
These children may not be as challenging

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:12.372
It's a catastrophe.

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.507
They are simply too young to understand.

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:17.276
But just like other than her family,

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:19.345
their lives have been changed forever

00:06:19.612 --> 00:06:21.280
by the earthquake.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:26.753
And now there is still mounting pressure

00:06:26.753 --> 00:06:27.720
on the Turkish government.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.521
There are still further

00:06:28.521 --> 00:06:30.423
calls for international support

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:32.725
and just over the weekend and today, U.S.

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:34.660
State Antony Blinken was visiting

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.963
those affected areas, announcing

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.264
further funding support

00:06:38.264 --> 00:06:39.565
for the humanitarian relief

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.200
effort from the US government,

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.771
now totaling about $180 million

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:45.571
to both Turkey

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:48.908
and Syria in support of that aid effort.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:49.609
But of course

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:51.244
the destruction is widespread.

00:06:51.244 --> 00:06:51.978
This is a process

00:06:51.978 --> 00:06:53.346
that is going to take months,

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:54.447
if not years,

00:06:54.447 --> 00:06:56.149
and that need for international support

00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:58.351
is only going to grow. Linda.

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:58.684
All right.

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.720
Not a big share for us in Adana Turkey.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.854
Thanks so much for that report.

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:03.389
We will bring you more details

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:04.590
on that latest earthquake

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.758
to hit the Turkish-Syrian

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:07.693
border as it comes to hand.

